Vector

It is predefined class present in java.util package that implements the list interface 
it has all the features of list 
it was introduced in JDK 1.0 (It is Lagecy class)
Just like arraylist the underlying datastructure is Growable/Resizable array
It maintainans memory location like arrays
it has default initial capacity of 10
the default incremental capacity is 2x
Vector is Thread safe (Syncronized) and this is why it is slower than Arraylist
